CORE
main.cpp
--cpp20
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ empty-pack call expands to base\(\): SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^.*found no match for symbol.*$
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
[temp.variadic]/5 -- expanding an empty parameter pack in a function-call
argument list yields an empty argument list, so `base(a...)` with zero pack
elements is the call `base()`.  Fixed by the unified pack-expansion rework
(Phase 1): the empty-pack body call-argument stripping in instantiate_template
now recovers the function parameter pack's name from the original template when
the (empty) pack parameter has already been removed from the instantiated
declaration, so its call-argument references are stripped.
